│                                                                              │
│  Remediation                                                                 │
│  Enforce the missing invariant at the two points where the fragment state    │
│  is produced and consumed. When a fragment is stored, reject any datagram    │
│  for which the running total of fragment lengths would exceed the declared   │
│  message length, and size the reassembly buffer to exactly the declared      │
│  length rather than `data_length * sizeof(char *)`. When the reassembled     │
│  message is handed to the parser, additionally verify that the accumulated   │
│  length is non-negative, no larger than the declared length, and no larger   │
│  than `DTLS_MAX_FRAGMENT_SIZE` before it is used as a copy length into the   │
│  fixed stack buffer. Both bounds can be derived from the peer's own          │
│  handshake header, which is already capped at `DTLS_MAX_FRAGMENT_SIZE`, so   │
│  no additional negotiation is required. As defence in depth, move the 256    │
│  KiB `local_buffer` in `tls_parse_payload` off the stack or allocate it      │
│  once per context, and add regression coverage for fragmented DTLS           │
│  handshakes, which the project currently lacks.                              │
│                                                                              │
