│  Remediation                                                                 │
│  Implement the anti-replay window that RFC 6347 section 4.1.2.6 requires     │
│  for every DTLS context: retain the highest authenticated record sequence    │
│  number together with a bitmap covering the preceding records (512 records   │
│  is the usual size), drop any record that is older than the window or whose  │
│  bit is already set, and advance the window only after the record's AEAD     │
│  tag has verified so that forged datagrams cannot move it. Sequence numbers  │
│  must be compared per direction and per epoch, and the window must reset     │
│  when the epoch advances. Records rejected as duplicates should be           │
│  discarded silently rather than answered with an alert, so that a replayed   │
│  datagram does not produce an error response an attacker can use as an       │
│  oracle. If contexts are exported and imported between processes in the      │
│  middle of a DTLS association, serialize the window state as well, or        │
│  document that the receiving process starts with an empty window.            │
│                                                                              │
